# Kemp eliminase theozyme: Asp general base + Gln oxyanion donor + 6NT.
# Generated by scripts/make_enzdes_cst.py - do not hand-edit.
#
# Targets are the CRYSTAL-measured values in kemp/official.py TARGETS
# (4BS0/7K4Z), with tolerances set from the scoring windows. The
# denovoKemp constraint numbers are NOT used: their base contacts a
# ring CARBON on the substrate, ours contacts a ring NITROGEN on the
# TSA, so the values do not transfer (LOOP_DESIGN 3.2).
#
# Rosetta enzdes atom convention (A = ligand, B = protein):
#   distanceAB A1-B1   angle_A A2-A1-B1   angle_B A1-B1-B2
#   torsion_A A3-A2-A1-B1   torsion_AB A2-A1-B1-B2   torsion_B A1-B1-B2-B3
#
# columns: target  tolerance  penalty_k  periodicity  n_samples

# catalytic base: Asp carboxylate to 6NT N3
#   measured on the theozyme: d=2.482 A, angle_A=124.64, torsion_AB=328.13
CST::BEGIN
  TEMPLATE::   ATOM_MAP: 1 atom_name: N3 N2 N1
  TEMPLATE::   ATOM_MAP: 1 residue3: 6NT
  TEMPLATE::   ATOM_MAP: 2 atom_name: OD2 CG OD1
  TEMPLATE::   ATOM_MAP: 2 residue1: D

  CONSTRAINT:: distanceAB:    2.52   0.30   100.0  0     1
  CONSTRAINT::    angle_A:  120.00  20.00    60.0  360.  1
  CONSTRAINT:: torsion_AB:  339.90  40.00    60.0  360.  1
CST::END

# oxyanion donor: Gln amide to 6NT N1
#   measured on the theozyme: d=3.331 A, angle_A=124.83, torsion_AB=50.90
CST::BEGIN
  TEMPLATE::   ATOM_MAP: 1 atom_name: N1 N2 N3
  TEMPLATE::   ATOM_MAP: 1 residue3: 6NT
  TEMPLATE::   ATOM_MAP: 2 atom_name: NE2 CD OE1
  TEMPLATE::   ATOM_MAP: 2 residue1: Q

  CONSTRAINT:: distanceAB:    3.10   0.30   100.0  0     1
  CONSTRAINT::    angle_A:  120.00  20.00    60.0  360.  1
  CONSTRAINT:: torsion_AB:  359.20  40.00    60.0  360.  1
CST::END
